  "$comment": "HINT TABLE ONLY. Maps a marketing carrier's flight-number block to the regional operator that probably flies it, so the DesignatorResolver can look for an existing FlightTracker before spending a provider call. The provider's operating carrier is always authoritative; a wrong hint costs one cache miss, never a wrong key. packages/db seeds the regional_operators table from OPTD and overrides this file. Airlines do not publish per-operator blocks: 'published' means a third-party reference page (cptdb.ca wiki, a dated enthusiast post) states the block, 'observed' means it was inferred from dated flight records or forum posts, 'assumed' means a conservative guess that the increment 2 result lists as unverified. Ranges are deliberately narrow where sources disagree; a number outside every block simply gets no hint.",
